findings.evidence:
parse_message takes From from the header (mail.py:246-253). Nothing in app/ reads Authentication-Results, DKIM, SPF or DMARC (grep finds none). These all rest on emails.from_addr:
- `has_written` (mailstore.py:220-227);
- `never.reasons` first_contact (never.py:63, :90-94);
- the database's own NEVER view (0051_never.sql:21, recreated in 0054_pinterest.sql:165);
- `policy._started_by_them` (policy.py:79-90);
- the card's first_contact flag (views.py:749);
- the tool's §7 warning (tools.py:3167).
The code layer and the database layer check the same unauthenticated signal.

agenda.py:102-106 makes any email whose In-Reply-To/References names a Message-ID Ember sent an urgent 'reply'. It skips the bulk, machine and suppression filters that the inquiry branch uses (:107-112 via mailstore.inquiries). service.py:343-361 wakes on it: at most 4 a day, 30 minutes apart. The inquiry filter is itself narrow:
- machine() knows 4 local-part prefixes (mailstore.py:233-238);
- `_bulk` reads only the List-*, Precedence and Auto-Submitted headers (mail.py:283-290);
- spam headers and the provider's authentication verdict are never read.

obligations.py:180 and agenda.py:95 call `mailstore.inquiries(conn, scope)` without `own`, so it compares against '' (mailstore.py:249-260); `is_inquiry` (:263-264) does the same. Every way to clear such an email refuses Ember's own address:
- `inquiry_done` passes box.address (tools.py:3113-3114) and refuses;
- `mark_opt_out` refuses (tools.py:3099-3100);
- `propose_email` refuses (tools.py:3163-3164).
`counts()` (mailstore.py:275-286) has no machine, own or suppression filter, although DOCS.md:1020-1022 says bounces and no-reply senders don't count.
